<!--
  COLOUR FOREGROUND of the adaptive icon: the CafePos mark, as a vector.

  Same role as before: this file and cafepos_icon_monochrome.xml carry byte-identical
  pathData so the colour layer and the themed layer can be diffed. Keep that invariant.
  The colour mark has no interior detail, which is what lets one geometry serve both
  jobs; the moment the colour layer grows a feature the tint cannot carry, the
  monochrome file has to be redrawn separately.

  CANVAS AND MEASURED EXTREMES (radius from the canvas centre, 54,54)
  =================================================================
  The mark is designed to the 72dp MASKABLE zone (the guaranteed-visible area once the
  launcher has applied its mask), not the 66dp guaranteed-visible-UNMASKED zone.

    element                          point        radius
    steam A top-cap LEFT corner      (43.5, 25.5)  30.373   <- BINDING
    steam A top-cap top              (45, 25.5)    29.89
    steam B top-cap left corner      (52.5, 25.5)  28.54
    saucer left cap                  (36, 76)      28.43
    saucer right cap                 (71, 76)      27.80
    cup rim left                     (34, 42)      23.32
    handle outer right               (72.15, 51.5) 18.32
    handle outer top                 (64.65, 44)   14.61
    cup base                         (47, 71)      18.39

  MAX RADIUS = 30.373, so the mark is 60.75 across. That leaves
      2.63 units inside the 33.0 guaranteed-visible-unmasked zone, and
      5.63 units inside the 36.0 maskable hard limit.
  (This revision is SMALLER than the previous max radius of 31.83, even though the
  steam got much taller, because narrowing the saucer gave back the room the steam
  needed. See SAUCER below.)

  HANDLE: WHY r 5.75 / stroke 3.5
  =============================
  Ring outer diameter 15.0 against a 26.0-wide cup = 57.7%, which is what a cup
  handle actually looks like. It was 22.0 against the same cup (85%), which is why the
  icon read as a cup with a bagel strapped to it. Counter diameter 8.0, still an
  obviously open hole and still real negative space, which is the entire reason the
  handle is a ring and not a filled outline.

  Two clearances, both recomputed at the new size, against the cup's right wall
  (the line through (60,42) and (56.5,64)):

    perpendicular distance from ring centre to that wall   d = 6.085
    MERGE    ring's left arc sits INSIDE the cup wall     7.500 - 6.085 = 1.415
    CLEARANCE counter stays clear of the cup wall          6.085 - 4.000 = 2.085

  These two numbers are not independent, and that is worth knowing before anyone
  "improves" one of them. A wall crossing a ring band splits the band, so

      merge + clearance == stroke width        (1.415 + 2.085 == 3.5)

  holds exactly. With the 2-unit floor on the negative space, a 3.5 stroke caps the
  merge at 1.5 no matter where the ring is placed. The clearance was set to 2.085
  (just over the floor) precisely to hand the rest of the band to the merge. A 1.415
  unit merge is not a hairline: the buried arc is +/-35.8 degrees, 9.37 units of
  circumference, because the wall is near-vertical and crosses the band square-on.

  Ring top is y 44.0, which is 2.0 units BELOW the cup rim at y 42. The old ring top
  was y 41, i.e. 1.0 unit above the rim, and that peek over the rim was a large part of
  the bagel look. Ring bottom y 59.0, clear of the cup base (71) and the saucer (73).

  STEAM: WHY 11 TALL ON A 3 STROKE
  ===============================
  Each curl is 11.0 units tall on a 3.0 stroke, a 3.67:1 ratio, so the stroke is 27%
  of the curl height and the path is not swallowed by its own line weight. The previous
  curls were 5.0 tall on a 5.0 stroke, a 1:1 ratio: the stroke filled the path and the
  render was an 8x10 rounded lozenge, which is why they read as two tick marks.
  Two curls, not three. Bottom caps stop at y 39.5, a 2.5 gap below the rim, and the
  two curls are 4.0 apart.

  SAUCER: NARROWED, RE-CENTRED, GAP CUT
  =====================================
  35.0 wide (was 42.0), spanning x 36..71, thickness 6.0, y 73..79.
    overhang left of the cup   2.0
    overhang right of the cup  11.0   (was 14.0, and it reached out under the handle)
  Centred at x 53.5, against a cup+handle mass of x 34..72.15 centred at 53.08, so the
  overhang is now balanced under the whole silhouette instead of only under the cup.
  The handle extends 1.15 past the saucer's right edge, which is how a cup on a saucer
  looks. The gap from the cup base (71) to the saucer top (73) is 2.0, was 3.0, so the
  cup now sits on the saucer rather than hovering over it.

  EVERY FLOOR, STATED
  ===================
  Nothing is below the 2-unit (2dp) floor:
    steam stroke 3.0, handle stroke 3.5, saucer thickness 6.0
    counter diameter 8.0, counter-to-cup-wall 2.085
    steam-to-rim 2.5, curl-to-curl 4.0, cup-to-saucer 2.0
  The one number below 2 is the 1.415 handle merge, and that is a connection, not a
  stroke and not a gap. It is bounded above by the stroke width as shown above.

  Thumbnail: contrast of #F2C14E on #143D59 is 6.8:1.
  No baked-in mask and no drop shadow; the launcher supplies its own mask and shadow.
  The saucer's 3dp semicircular caps are cubics, not arcs, so nothing here needs arc
  support below API 24. The handle circle is four cubics for the same reason.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- cup body: 26.0 wide, y 42..71. Unchanged by this revision. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F2C14E"
        android:pathData="M34,42 L60,42 L56.5,64 C55.4,68.7 51.6,71 47,71 C42.4,71 38.6,68.7 37.5,64 Z" />

    <!--
      handle: a ring, i.e. a stroked circle with no fill, so its 8.0 counter is genuine
      negative space that survives being flattened to a single colour.
      centre (64.65, 51.5), r 5.75, stroke 3.5; four cubics, k = 0.5523 * 5.75 = 3.18.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#F2C14E"
        android:strokeWidth="3.5"
        android:pathData="M64.65,45.75 C67.83,45.75 70.4,48.32 70.4,51.5 C70.4,54.68 67.83,57.25 64.65,57.25 C61.47,57.25 58.9,54.68 58.9,51.5 C58.9,48.32 61.47,45.75 64.65,45.75 Z" />

    <!-- steam: two curls, 11.0 tall on a 3.0 stroke, 4.0 apart, 2.5 clear of the rim -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#F2C14E"
        android:strokeWidth="3"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:pathData="M43,38 C40.8,33.5 45.2,31.5 45,27" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:strokeColor="#F2C14E"
        android:strokeWidth="3"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:pathData="M52,38 C49.8,33.5 54.2,31.5 54,27" />

    <!-- saucer: 35.0 wide rounded bar, y 73..79, 2.0 clear of the cup base -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F2C14E"
        android:pathData="M39,73 L68,73 C69.66,73 71,74.34 71,76 C71,77.66 69.66,79 68,79 L39,79 C37.34,79 36,77.66 36,76 C36,74.34 37.34,73 39,73 Z" />
</vector>
